# Applies to builds that use frontend/Dockerfile.
#
# The backend has had one of these for a while; the frontend did not, so it fell
# back to the root .dockerignore — which excludes only a top-level `node_modules`
# and `.git`. Two consequences, both real:
#
# 1. `COPY frontend/ .` copied `frontend/.env` into the image. Only a feature
#    flag today, but nothing stopped the next value added there from being a
#    secret, and a value baked into a layer is in the image forever.
# 2. The build context was 210MB, almost all of it `frontend/node_modules` and
#    `backend/node_modules` being shipped to the daemon on every build, only to
#    be overwritten by `npm install` a moment later.
#
# Patterns are relative to the BUILD CONTEXT root, which docker-compose sets to
# the repo root — not to frontend/. That is why every rule below is written with
# `**/` rather than as a bare filename.
#
# Configuration reaches the app at runtime from the backend (GET /auth-config),
# never by being copied in.

**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
.git/

# Build output — regenerated inside the image, and stale copies only confuse.
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# Test and CI material: not needed to build or serve the app.
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
frontend/e2e/
frontend/tests/
backend/tests/
